rd i understood not then  but now i know it means dancing  then came all the women who were in the  seven huts and seized hold of me and the  men went away  several of the women led me along by the  arms and several by the ropes which were  bound around my neck so roughly and  tightly that i could hardly breathe and  i knew not what they intended to do with  me upon which i tried to remember the  sufferings of our lord jesus christ and  how he suffered innocently whereby i  consoled myself and became more resigned  i asked whether they were going to kill  me then when they answered  not yet  upon which a woman came out from the  crowd towards me holding a fragment of  crystal and with this same piece of  crystal shaved off my eyebrows i would  also have cut the beard from my chin but  this i would not suffer and said that  they should kill me with my beard  two women were with me and they tied to  one of my legs strings of objects which  rattled  thereupon the woman-kind all began  together to sing and to their time i was  obliged to stamp with their leg to which  they had tied the rattles so that they  rattled  in harmony  eventually i was handed over to  iperowasu who kept me in careful custody  he told me that i still had some time to  live and they brought all their gods  that were in the huts and placed them  around me and said that those had  prophesied that they would capture a  portuguese  then said i these things have no power  and also cannot speak and they lie in  asserting that i am portuguese for i am  one of the frenchman's allies and  friends and the country where i am at  home to which i belong is called germany  they knew full well that the frenchman  were just as much the enemies of the  portuguese as they for the frenchmen  came every year with ships and brought  them knives axes looking glasses combs  and scissors therefore they were good  friends which the portuguese had not  been they further said that the  portuguese had shot the father of the