and told me how they had  been stricken with illness and that i  had well known it for he still  remembered that i had said the moon  looked angrily towards his huts  when i heard these words from him i  thought to myself  surely it must be through god's  providence that i last night as a four  said spoke about the moon  i was in great joy at this and i thought  today  god is with me  and so i told him that it was true  because he wanted to eat me though i was  not his enemy and therefore had  misfortune come upon him  upon which he said that nothing should  happen to me if it turned out that he  recovered  i knew not how best to pray to god and  thought if they regain health they will  yet kill me but if they die the others  will say let us kill him before more  misfortune happens on this account  so i submitted the matter to god  chipipo begged me hard that they might  again recover i walked round them and  laid my hands upon their heads as they  desired me to do  but god would not have it so  they began  to die  first died one of their children then  his mother died an old woman who was  baking the pots wherein were to be made  the beverages with which i was to be  eaten she also died after some days one  of his brothers died then another child  and another brother and so on now when  he saw that his children his mother and  his brothers were gone he feared much  that he and his wives would also die  he said that i was to tell my god to  withdraw his anger so that he might live  i of course comforted him and told him  there was no danger but that when he  recovered again he was not to think of  killing me  thereupon he answered  no and also commanded those in the huts  that nobody should injure me or threaten  to eat me  he nevertheless remained ill for a time  but he was at last restored to health  together with one of his wives who was  also ill  there died however about eight of his  friends besides others who had treated  me cruelly  now there were yet two other kings from  two other huts  one had dreamt that i appeared before  him and had told him that he was to die  i said no he was not to be afraid but  that he also was not to think of killing  me or advise others to do it  in like manner the other king had also  dreamt of me a dream which had terrified  him much and he called me to his hut and  then complained of it to me and said he  had once been to war and had captured a  portuguese and had killed him with his  own hands and had eaten of him so  plentifully that his chest or stomach  had ever since been delicate and he  declared that he would eat of no other  him also i paid to be of good cheer but  he was to take care never to eat human  flesh again  [Music]  thus they  left me alone for a while not knowing  quite what to make of me whether i was a  portuguese or a frenchman  they said i had a red beard like a  frenchman and though they had also seen  portuguese yet these had all black  beards  and so when the frenchman came again to  the huts he spoke to me in the savage  tongue and at that time i went about  unfettered then he asked me if i still  lived and i said yes i thanked god that  he had preserved me for so long and i  called him privately to a spot where the  savages could not hear what i said and  told him that he saw plainly that god  had preserved my life  but also that i was no portuguese  but a german and i asked if he had not a  christian heart in his bosom or had  thought that after this life there was  no other when he had strongly advised  that i should be killed  and so according to my request he told  the savages that he had not well  recognized me the first time but that i  was from germany and belonged to their  friends and that he wanted to take me  with him to where the ships generally  arrived  my masters  said no they would not give me up for  they had found me in the enemy's country  and i belonged  to them  it happened after several days that they  wanted to eat a prisoner in a village  nearby about six miles from where i lay  imprisoned  on the eve of this day when they  intended drinking to his death i went to  him and said to him  everything is prepared for thy death  he laughed and he said  yes  further i told him he was to be of good  cheer for they would only eat his flesh  but his soul would proceed to another  place without our countrymen's souls  also proceeded and where there was much  happiness  he then asked me if this was really true  i said yes  but  quoth he he'd never seen god  and i said  he would see him  in the next life  there was one more incident before i  escaped now among them was a slave  belonging to a tribe called the cario  who are also enemies of the savages that  are friends of the portuguese  so it happened about the year 1554  during the sixth month of my captivity  that the cario fell sick and his master  who owned him begged me to help him that  he might be well again and catch game  bringing something for us to eat but  that if i thought he would not recover  again he would give him to a good friend  who might kill him and gain a name by  him i tried but finally they said he  will die we will therefore before he  dies strike him dead i said no do not do  this he may perhaps recover  but it veiled not they dragged him  before the hutts and two of them held  him for he was so sick that he knew not  what they were going to do with him and  so came the one whom he had been given  to kill and struck him on the head so  that the brain sprang out  then they left him lying before the huts  and wished to eat him i told them not to  do this as he had been sick and they  might also fall ill therefore they knew  not what to do  but one of them came out the hut wherein  i was and called to the women to make a  fire near the dead man  and he cut his head off  then he cut him up and divided him  equally with the others as is their  custom and ate him all but the head and  bowels of which they had a loathing as  the man had been sick  i went now and again through the  different huts in one they broiled the  feet in another the hands and in the  third pieces of the trunk  then i told them how the carrier whom  they were broiling  and were going to eat had at all times  lied against me and had said that i had  shot several of their friends when i was  with the portuguese and in this he had  lied and he had never seen me  you know well i continued that he was  several years among you and never was  ill but now on account of the lies which  he told about me my god has become angry  and has stricken him with sickness and  has put into your minds that you should  kill him and eat him so will my god do  unto all wicked men who have worked me  harm  and who would further injure me  at such words  they were much terrified  it happened that one day some savages  came to me and said that they had heard  of firing which must be at itaron the  harbour also called rio de janeiro  hearing with certainty that a ship was  there i told them that they were to take  me to it as probably my brothers would  be there  eventually the news was brought to me by  the savages the two men from the ship  had arrived there i was overjoyed and  went to them and bade them welcome in  the savage tongue  when they saw me in such a wretched  plight they had pity upon me and divided  their garments with me  i asked them why they had come they  answered on my account as they had been  commanded to take me to the ship and to  affect this they were to use every means  and so i said to one of the two who knew  the language of the savages that he had  to feign the following he was to be my  brother and he was to make believe that  i would remain among them and collect  pepper and other produce until the ships  returned the next year about 10 sailors  who in some degree resembled me should  come together and state that they were  my brothers and wanted to carry me home  with them my false brothers should in no  way consent that 